{"timestamp": 1783629922.746144, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 16, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1783629937.7963011, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I reported Charlie\u2019s body in cafeteria.\n\nMy route this round was electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria. In electrical around tick 4, I saw Bob enter from security, and Diana also entered electrical from medbay. I then went to medbay. Around tick 6, Bob came into medbay from electrical, and at tick 7 he left medbay toward upper_engine.\n\nI never saw Diana again after electrical, and now she\u2019s dead there, so Bob was the last person I personally saw near her \u2014 but I did not witness a kill. I also don\u2019t have any info on Charlie before finding his body in cafeteria. Didn\u2019t see Alice or Frank this round."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629957.341316, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Yeah, Eve\u2019s timeline is mostly right except the implication on Diana is a little unfair. I did go security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 cafeteria, then back toward medbay. In electrical I saw both Eve and Diana there, but I didn\u2019t stay \u2014 I left and later saw Eve in medbay too.\n\nThe important part: I saw Charlie alive in cafeteria around tick 12, coming in from weapons. I didn\u2019t see a body there when I passed through, so Charlie died after that. Eve is the one reporting him in cafeteria, and she was also one of the last people around electrical with Diana before Diana disappeared. That doesn\u2019t prove it\u2019s Eve, but I don\u2019t think \u201cBob was near Diana\u201d is enough when Eve was literally on that route too.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Alice or Frank at all, so I\u2019d like to hear from them before we lock anything."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629975.037775, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I was nowhere near either body. My route was security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower_engine. I saw Bob in security at tick 1 \u2014 he came in from weapons. Then I saw Charlie alive in navigation around tick 3, and at tick 4 Charlie left navigation toward security. Later I saw Frank in lower_engine around tick 11.\n\nSo for Charlie: I can confirm he was alive early and heading security, and Bob\u2019s claim that Charlie was later alive in cafeteria around tick 12 could fit if Charlie looped around from security/weapons to cafeteria. I didn\u2019t see Eve or Diana at all.\n\nThe two people with actual proximity to both stories are Bob and Eve, based on what they\u2019re saying. Eve found Charlie, and both Eve/Bob were around electrical where Diana was last seen. I don\u2019t have enough to hard accuse yet, but I really want to hear Frank\u2019s route because right now this is mostly between Bob and Eve unless Frank saw something important."}}
{"timestamp": 1783630004.05686, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I didn\u2019t see either body, so my hard info is limited. My route was upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 back through upper_engine \u2192 lower_engine \u2192 storage. The only person I saw was Alice at tick 11 in lower_engine, and I saw her enter lower_engine from storage. That matches her story, so I\u2019m fairly comfortable Alice wasn\u2019t around electrical for Diana, at least.\n\nFor me this really does come down to Bob vs Eve. Both of them put themselves on the electrical/medbay/upper_engine/oxygen/cafeteria line, which connects both deaths. The part that sticks out is Diana: Eve says she left Diana in electrical with Bob nearby, then Bob shows up in medbay a bit later. That gives Bob a pretty clear window on Diana. For Charlie, Bob\u2019s claim that he saw Charlie alive in cafeteria around tick 12 could be true, but it could also just be him trying to control the timeline since he admits being there.\n\nEve reporting Charlie could be a self-report, sure, but Bob is the one who seems to have proximity to both Diana and Charlie by his own route and Eve\u2019s route. I\u2019m leaning Bob here more than Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1783630020.64402, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "After hearing everyone, I\u2019m still leaning Bob.\n\nMy key info is Diana: at tick 4, Diana came into electrical from medbay, Bob came into electrical from security, and I left toward medbay. Then at tick 6 Bob came into medbay from electrical. That gives Bob a window alone near Diana, and Diana is now dead.\n\nFor Charlie, I found the body in cafeteria. Bob says he saw Charlie alive there around tick 12, which means Bob was also on that side of the map near Charlie\u2019s death window. Alice and Frank seem to vouch for each other being lower_engine/storage area, away from both bodies.\n\nSo from my perspective, Bob has proximity to both deaths, especially Diana. I think Bob is the best vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1783630039.0902982, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I need to push back here because this is turning into \u201cBob was nearby so Bob,\u201d but Eve was on the exact same corridor line and is the only person actually found with a body.\n\nFor Diana: yes, I was in electrical briefly. I saw Eve there first, then Diana there. Eve keeps framing it like I was alone with Diana, but she was also in that room/route and then we both end up medbay/upper_engine/oxygen side. Nobody actually found Diana\u2019s body location this meeting, so saying \u201cDiana died in electrical\u201d is an assumption based on last seen, not proof.\n\nFor Charlie: my info is that Charlie entered cafeteria from weapons at tick 12 and was alive. I did not report because there was no body when I passed through. Eve reports Charlie in cafeteria after that. That means the freshest hard proximity to a confirmed body is Eve, not me.\n\nAlice and Frank seem away from this based on lower_engine/storage matching. So yeah, I agree it\u2019s between me and Eve, but I think Eve is using the Diana timeline to distract from the fact she reported Charlie exactly where I last saw him alive. I\u2019m voting Eve unless someone has something stronger."}}
{"timestamp": 1783630071.965699, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m still seeing this as Bob versus Eve, but I lean Bob.\n\nMy own info clears me and mostly clears Frank from the main route: I was security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower_engine, saw Bob in security tick 1, Charlie alive in navigation tick 3 leaving toward security tick 4, and Frank in lower_engine tick 11. Frank\u2019s route matches what I saw, and neither of us were near electrical or cafeteria.\n\nThe Diana part is what matters most to me. Eve\u2019s timeline has Bob entering electrical from security right as Diana came in from medbay, then Bob shows up in medbay a little later. That is a very clean window for Bob to have killed Diana. Bob is right that we don\u2019t know the exact body location, but Diana was last seen there with him nearby.\n\nFor Charlie, Eve reporting could be a self-report, but Bob also places himself in cafeteria around Charlie\u2019s death window and is the one giving the \u201cI saw him alive at tick 12\u201d timeline. That doesn\u2019t clear him.\n\nSo between the two, Bob has the stronger proximity to both deaths. I\u2019m voting Bob unless Frank has something that changes it."}}
{"timestamp": 1783630081.719899, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I don\u2019t have new hard info beyond what I already said: my route was upper_engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper_engine \u2192 lower_engine \u2192 storage, and the only person I saw was Alice at tick 11 in lower_engine, entering from storage. That matches her route, so I\u2019m comfortable that Alice is not the duck here.\n\nSo it\u2019s still Bob versus Eve for me. I agree with Alice: Diana is the stronger point. Eve\u2019s story puts Bob entering electrical right as Diana is there, then Bob later coming out toward medbay. That\u2019s a clean kill window, and Diana is dead now. Bob\u2019s defense is basically \u201cEve was nearby too,\u201d but Eve left toward medbay before Bob showed up there.\n\nFor Charlie, yes, Eve reported the body, so self-report is possible. But Bob also admits being in cafeteria around Charlie\u2019s death window and claims he saw Charlie alive there. That doesn\u2019t clear him \u2014 it keeps him in the area for both deaths.\n\nAlice and I seem away from both bodies. Between Bob and Eve, Bob has the better opportunity on Diana and still has proximity to Charlie. I\u2019m voting Bob."}}
